    "https://www.webber.edu/career-services/": {
      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Career Services - Webber International University Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility LIVE WEBBER SPORTS Current Students Brightspace Student Information Services Handbooks Catalogs Policies and Procedures Schedules & Calendars Webber Email Registrar Order a Diploma Order a Transcript Learning Resource Center The Learning Commons Jobs @ Webber Events Alumni Giving LIVE WEBBER SPORTS Current Students Brightspace Student Information Services Handbooks Catalogs Policies and Procedures Schedules & Calendars Webber Email Registrar Order a Diploma Order a Transcript Learning Resource Center The Learning Commons Jobs @ Webber Events Alumni Giving LIVE WEBBER SPORTS Current Students Brightspace Student Information Services Handbooks Catalogs Policies and Procedures Schedules & Calendars Webber Email Registrar Order a Diploma Order a Transcript Learning Resource Center The Learning Commons Jobs @ Webber Events Alumni Giving On Campus Programs Undergraduate Business Programs Accounting Computer Information Systems Data Analytics Artificial Intelligence Computer Science and Technology Criminal Justice Management Finance General Business Studies Hospitality & Tourism Management Integrated Marketing Communications Management Sport Business Management Undergraduate Health Profession Programs Health Services Administration Bachelor of Science in Nursing Bachelor of Science in Occupational Therapy Assistant Psychology Sports Performance, Health, & Fitness Undergraduate Education Programs Elementary Education Middle Grades Teacher Education Special Education Graduate Programs Traditional MBA MBA: Accounting MBA: Criminal Justice Management MBA: International Business MBA: Sport Business Management Online Programs Undergraduate Online Programs Accounting Computer Information Systems Data Analytics Artificial Intelligence Computer Science and Technology Criminal Justice Management Finance General Business Studies Hospitality & Tourism Management Integrated Marketing Communications Management Psychology Sport Business Management Graduate Online Program Master of Arts Degree in Education: Instructional Design and Curricular Supervision Traditional MBA MBA: Accounting MBA: Criminal Justice Management MBA: International Business MBA: Sport Business Management Online Education MedCerts Zschools State Authorization and Professional Licensure Student Services Academic Support Career Services Clubs & Activities Housing & Residential Life University Life Admissions & Financial Aid Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Students Accepted Students Financial Aid Military Tuition & Fees Net Price Calculator Veterans Education Benefits Schedule A Visit International Students Athletics About Webber History Mission Faculty & Staff Campus Map Shop @ Webber Institutional Effectiveness & Research Title IX Information Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Community Outreach Consumer Information ICUF EASE Performance Measures Our Career Services office is committed to helping you navigate your path to professional success. Whether you’re exploring potential career paths, preparing for your first job, or seeking guidance on advancing your career, we offer personalized support and valuable resources. From career assessments and resume building to networking events and employer connections, our goal is to equip you with the tools and skills you need to thrive in today’s competitive job market. We’re here to support you every step of the way—start your journey with us today! Career Services: Your Pathway to Success Preparing You for a Bright Future, One Step at a Time Career Services Overview Career Closet Handshake Internship & Volunteer Opportunities Job Fairs & Employer Networking Events Licensure Information for Students Professional Development Workshops Information for Employers Career Services Overview The Career Services Office at Webber International University is dedicated to supporting both current students and alumni in their professional development and career preparation. From the moment you arrive on campus, our goal is to help you navigate the path to a successful career by providing valuable resources, guidance, and connections. We offer personalized support, including: Career Assessments : Gain insights into your strengths, interests, and career possibilities through various assessments that help you better understand your professional path. Resume and Cover Letter Development : Craft a polished, professional resume and cover letter that stand out to employers. Interview Preparation : Build confidence through mock interviews and personalized feedback to sharpen your interview skills. Networking Opportunities : Connect with potential employers through on-campus recruitment events, employer visits, and our annual career fair. We are committed to helping you succeed, whether you’re looking to secure an internship, prepare for your first job, or advance in your chosen field.  At Webber, your future is our priority, and we’re here to support you every step of the way. Current or former students with access to Webber email can book an appointment online at: The Learning Commons Bookings Career Closet At Webber International University, we understand that the right outfit can make all the difference when preparing for a class presentation, interview, or career fair. That’s why we’re thrilled to introduce our Career Closet —a valuable resource designed to provide students in need with stylish and professional business attire! Need to Borrow? If you’re looking for that perfect outfit to make a lasting impression, head over to our Career Closet! Students can borrow business attire by visiting the FBLA advisor, Academic Affairs, or Career Services . Our friendly staff is ready to assist you in selecting the perfect ensemble that fits your style and needs. Want to Contribute? If you’re looking to make a difference, consider donating to our Career Closet! Clean, gently used business attire can be dropped off with any of the aforementioned individuals. Your contributions will not only help fellow students dress for success but also foster a sense of community and support within our university. Each donated item will be carefully inventoried to ensure our closet remains stocked and ready for those who need it. Let’s work together to empower every Webber student to present their best selves! For more information, feel free to reach out to Career Services or stop by to explore our collection. Handshake What is Handshake? Handshake is a powerful online platform designed to connect students and alumni with job opportunities, internships, and employers. It serves as a one-stop resource for finding career-related opportunities, managing applications, and building a professional network. Handshake is widely used by colleges and universities across the country, making it an essential tool for Webber International University students and alumni. Why Use Handshake? Handshake offers numerous benefits that make it a must-have resource for students and alumni at all stages of their career journey: Access to Opportunities : With thousands of job and internship postings, Handshake connects you with top employers actively looking for candidates from Webber. Tailored Job Recommendations : Handshake’s personalized approach ensures that you see job postings and opportunities that match your interests, skills, and experiences. Build Your Network : Handshake makes it easy to connect with employers, alumni, and fellow students, providing valuable networking opportunities. Easy Application Process : Seamlessly apply for jobs, internships, and on-campus employment directly through the platform. Getting started with Handshake early in your college journey helps you explore career paths, build your professional presence, and connect with employers who are eager to hire Webber students and alumni. Student Link For Employers If you’re an employer looking to hire talented students and alumni from Webber International University, Handshake is the ideal platform to post job openings and internships. By utilizing Handshake, you can reach a targeted pool of qualified candidates who are actively seeking professional opportunities. Posting your job on Handshake is easy and ensures that your positions are seen by students and alumni eager to make an impact in your organization. To get started, create an employer account on Handshake and start connecting with our students today. Employer Link Internship & Volunteer Opportunities Why Internships and Volunteer Opportunities Matter Gaining experience through internships and volunteer work is one of the most important steps you can take while in college. These opportunities allow you to apply what you’ve learned in the classroom to real-world settings, build your professional network, and develop skills that will set you apart from other graduates. It’s never too early to start—whether you’re just beginning your academic journey or nearing graduation, making time for these experiences will enhance your resume and give you a competitive edge in the job market. By taking on internships and volunteer work, you’ll also: Gain Practical Experience : These experiences help you put theory into practice and build confidence in your field of study. Expand Your Network : Internships and volunteer opportunities connect you with professionals who can offer mentorship, job leads, and career advice. Boost Your Resume : Employers seek candidates with not only a degree but also relevant experience. Internships and volunteer work will make you a standout candidate. Discover Your Passion : These opportunities allow you to explore different career paths and help you make informed decisions about your future. Finding Internship Opportunities At Webber, we encourage students to take advantage of every chance to gain hands-on experience. Internship opportunities can be found through Handshake , where employers actively seek Webber students for internships and job roles. Some opportunities may also be directly emailed from Career Services or shared by your program’s internship coordinator or faculty members . It’s important to explore these resources regularly to find opportunities that align with your career goals. If your degree program requires an internship for graduation, remember that you must meet all pre-requisites before using the internship for course credit. Additionally: Register for the Internship Course : You must be officially enrolled in the internship course. Get Approval Before Starting : Before beginning any internship that will count towards your degree, ensure you receive approval from your internship coordinator. Failure to meet these requirements will prevent the internship from counting toward your course credit, so make sure you follow the process correctly to gain the full benefit of the experience. By prioritizing internships and volunteer work during your time at Webber, you’ll set yourself up for success and ensure that you leave college with the degree—and the experience—that employers are looking for. Internship Coordinators for Internship Courses: Business (ACC, CIS, FIN, GBS, HTM, IMC, MGT): Professor David (DavidIM@webber.edu) Business (CJM): Dr. Barone (BaronePA@webber.edu) Business (SBM): Dr. Aaron (AaronTC@webber.edu) Psychology: Professor Harris (HarrisGE@webber.edu) Sports Performance, Health, & Fitness: Professor Zimmer (ZimmerES@webber.edu) Job Fairs & Employer Networking Events Job Fairs and Employer Networking Events: Why They Matter Participating in job fairs and employer networking events is one of the most valuable steps you can take in preparing for your future career. These events give you the chance to meet directly with potential employers, learn more about career opportunities in your field, and make meaningful professional connections. Taking these opportunities seriously and presenting yourself at your best is key—your first impression could lead to an internship, a job offer, or valuable advice that helps guide your career path. Job fairs and networking events are more than just meet-and-greets; they are opportunities to showcase your skills, ask important questions, and gain insights into what employers are looking for. Dress professionally, come prepared with a polished resume, and be ready to confidently discuss your goals and experiences. Annual Career Fair At Webber International University, we host an Annual Career Fair every fall, right here on campus. This event brings together a wide range of employers from various industries, providing students with the perfect platform to explore career paths, discuss internships, and learn about potential job openings. The career fair is an invaluable resource, helping you make direct connections with recruiters who are actively seeking new talent. Employer Networking on Campus In addition to the career fair, Webber regularly invites employers to set up booths on campus, giving students the chance to interact with industry professionals throughout the year. Employers are here to provide guidance on entering the workforce, discuss volunteer, internship, or job opportunities, and offer advice on career planning. These visits allow you to ask questions, explore potential career paths, and gain professional insight—all without leaving campus. These events are an essential part of your career preparation journey, and we encourage all students to take full advantage of them. Participating in job fairs and networking events can set you apart, open doors to new opportunities, and give you the confidence to succeed in your chosen field. Licensure Information for Students Navigating the path to professional licensure in Florida can be complex, as each field has specific requirements and regulations. This section provides essential information on various licensure options, including K-12 teaching certification, CPA exams, and healthcare-related licenses such as the BSN and occupational therapy assistant credentials. Understanding the requirements for each license is crucial for your career progression. Below are detailed resources to guide you through the application processes, eligibility criteria, and examination details for each licensure category in Florida. K-12 Teaching Certification in Florida : To become a certified teacher in Florida, you need to meet specific requirements set by the Florida Department of Education. This includes passing the Florida Teacher Certification Examinations (FTCE). You can find detailed information on certification pathways, required tests, and application processes on the Florida Department of Education’s website. More information is available here . Florida CPA Exam : The Florida Board of Accountancy manages the CPA Exam. Candidates must meet specific educational requirements and pass the Uniform CPA Examination. For more information on the application process, requirements, and resources for preparing for the exam, visit the Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation’s CPA page here. For a CPA Exam Review option, try Becker . ​ Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation License : Various professions are licensed under the Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation (DBPR). You can find information on how to apply for different licenses, renewal requirements, and related resources on their website here. Professional Development Workshops Professional Development Workshops: Your Key to Career Success It’s never too early to start working toward your career goals, and graduation will come sooner than you think! That’s why it’s so important to make time for professional development opportunities. These workshops provide the tools and knowledge you need to continuously improve and position yourself for success in today’s competitive job market. At Webber International University, Career Services hosts a variety of professional development workshops throughout the semesters to help you stay on track. From resume writing and cover letter crafting to mock interviews and networking strategies , these sessions are designed to help you sharpen your skills and build the confidence needed to excel in your chosen career. Taking advantage of these workshops will not only prepare you for life after graduation but will also give you the chance to continuously learn, grow, and stay ahead of the curve in your career journey. Make time for these essential events, and stay committed to your professional development every step of the way. Workshop notifications are emailed to your Webber email and posted to Brightspace as well as to the Student Life Instagram. Information for Employers Are you an employer interested in connecting with our students? Great! We are very flexible and are willing to set up the type of event that works best for you and your company. Some suggested ideas include: Connect with us on Handshake Host an Informational Session on campus (bonus points if you bring freebies!) Come out to our FREE Annual Career fair in the fall Have a representative from your company set up a Booth outside the classroom building (we will provide the table, chairs and tent) Hold on Campus Interviews for open positions If you’re interested in participating in one of the ideas above or if you just want to learn more about our students, fill out the contact form below so we can get in touch with you. Thank you for your interest in our students! 1201 North Scenic Highway Babson Park, FL 33827 863-638-1431 (Local) 1-800-741-1844 (Toll-Free) admissions@webber.edu Our Campus Institutional Effectiveness & Research Campus Safety Admissions Financial Aid Clubs & Activities International Students Athletics Title IX Information Newsletter ©2026 All Rights Reserved, Webber University | Designed and Built by Great Impressions , Privacy Policy admissions@webber.edu 1-800-741-1844 (Toll-Free) Accessibility, Cookie and Privacy Policy We use cookies to optimize our website and our service.In addition, if you are disabled or need any assistance navigating this website please use the UserWay feature on this website. Alternatively you can email us on info@webber.edu or call us on 863-638-1431 and one of our staff will provide you personalized support. Functional Functional Always active The technical storage or access is strictly necessary for the legitimate purpose of enabling the use of a specific service explicitly requested by the subscriber or user, or for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network. Preferences Preferences The technical storage or access is necessary for the legitimate purpose of storing preferences that are not requested by the subscriber or user. Statistics Statistics The technical storage or access that is used exclusively for statistical purposes. The technical storage or access that is used exclusively for anonymous statistical purposes. Without a subpoena, voluntary compliance on the part of your Internet Service Provider, or additional records from a third party, information stored or retrieved for this purpose alone cannot usually be used to identify you. Marketing Marketing The technical storage or access is required to create user profiles to send advertising, or to track the user on a website or across several websites for similar marketing purposes. Manage options Manage services Manage {vendor_count} vendors Read more about these purposes Accept Dismiss Preferences Save preferences Preferences {title} {title} {title} Manage consent"
