    "https://webber.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Nursing-Faculty-Job-Advertisement_2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Position: Full-time Nursing Faculty (Assistant Professor)",
      "description": " \nCollege of Health Professions & Sciences \n Bachelor of Science in Nursing \n \nPosition: Full-time Nursing Faculty (Assistant Professor) \nStatus: Full-Time 12 months \nLocation: Babson Park, Florida \nClosing Date: Open Until Filled \n \nWebber International University and the Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) Program invite applications for a \nfull-time nursing faculty position. The BSN Faculty reports directly to the Chief Nursing Administrator/Program \nDirector. These positions involve both administrative support and instructional responsibilities as appropriate \nwithin the program. Faculty will also serve as academic advisors to students as well as engage in scholarly \nactivities within the Nursing program and the College of Health Professions and Sciences. \n \nQualifications: \n• Master's degree in nursing required, preferably in nursing education or an earned doctorate degree \nfrom a regionally accredited institution in the teaching or professional discipline. \n• At least one-year previous college-level teaching experience \n• Three years full-time clinical experience in the area/areas of teaching responsibility \n• Current unrestricted State of Florida registered nursing license \n• Current CPR Healthcare Provider \n• Effective oral and written communication skills \n \nRoles and Responsibilities \n• Provide instruction for assigned courses \n• Evaluate student outcomes \n• Assist in curriculum planning and course development \n• Advise and tutor students and evaluate academic progression of students \n• Maintain and communicate office hours to encourage regular and effective consultation with students \n• Demonstrate commitment to professional development \n• Participate in campus-wide and community service opportunities \n• Assist with recruitment of students \n• Assist in the process for obtaining and maintaining accreditation status \n• Remain current with trends, issues, and practices in nursing \n• Demonstrate teamwork and collaboration \n• Maintain accurate class and other records required by the University and College of Health Professions \nand Sciences \n• Submit attendance roster and grade reports \n• Create, encourage, and maintain an inclusive environment that respects multiple learning styles \n• Work effectively to meet the needs of diverse student populations \n• Use current and emerging technologies and alternative delivery methods to enhance student learning \n• Maintain positive working relationships with faculty, staff, and administration \n\n \n \n \n• Practice and promote academic excellence and scholarship \n• Participate in Webber activities to include committees, extracurricular activities, \ncurriculum development \n• Maintain current membership and involvement in a professional nursing organization \n• Other related duties, as assigned by the Nursing Program Director Other: Health and training \nrequirements for the position as stipulated by clinical agencies, including but not limited to \nimmunizations, titers, and CPR certification; excellent  interpersonal, written, and oral \npresentations skills; proven educational or administrative experience in critical thinking, \nproblem solving and judgment skills, and varied course delivery methodologies. \n \n \nHow to apply: \n \nEmail a copy of your Curriculum Vitae (CV), including a list of three professional reference s, transcripts, \nand a cover letter outlining your interest for the position and your qualifications to:  \nlendersv@webber.edu. Attachments should be PDF files "
    }
  },
